{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8e7ad9d02d7813e9cb52e1a13ad6925fe3112b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_0 = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb745f62ddf5625f47a60b8976c60faebcf74f43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/3155197c1e19f8baf4c5389af3efa64a6a5c928c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> be determined by the recurrence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d293888df7007ec4ada4b226a235ad82caf9d9f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u_{k+1} = 2u_k - 2u_k^2.\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This sequence tends to a limit; call it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. What is the least value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdccfccc047b6c8985ceea4d5d27e3bc9e4bab3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|u_k-L| \\le \\frac{1}{2^{1000}}?\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0523cb5b307ec9639e051358bf5774d085f08c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\: 10\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\: 87\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\: 123\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\: 329\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\: 401$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"416\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that terms of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79da2f827d433a6217245303bb888f37fa508b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> lie in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad63cf45c7cbd6fdd4ca4770d46865cea1c6b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(0,\\frac12\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"58\" height=\"45\" /> and are strictly increasing.\n</p><p>Since the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79da2f827d433a6217245303bb888f37fa508b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> tends to the limit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed22e596b436e3d8a18552fb7eb6c61ca1a11500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea88b7c60080e484d15b7c959b8113ffcdb65938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_{k+1}=u_k=L&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The given equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc17550bdc3e83e869538666f0af21fb60f8d1a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L=2L-2L^2,\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"19\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73d64c888b7a5cce399da07f54cc533409b6d363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L=\\frac12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The given inequality becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f7ae2572a401ea4b62faf59a17ca35459d0b5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12-\\frac{1}{2^{1000}} \\leq u_k \\leq \\frac12+\\frac{1}{2^{1000}},\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"37\" /> and we only need to consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/969ba4efd7c438789a5deb0ae75269ca4316917b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12-\\frac{1}{2^{1000}} \\leq u_k.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/665d690b5c0671da2c0d24055f163b8f3a04b5e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{8} u_0 &amp;= \\phantom{1}\\frac14 &amp;&amp;= \\frac{2^1-1}{2^2}, \\\\ u_1 &amp;= \\phantom{1}\\frac38 &amp;&amp;= \\frac{2^2-1}{2^3}, \\\\ u_2 &amp;= \\ \\frac{15}{32} &amp;&amp;= \\frac{2^4-1}{2^5}, \\\\ u_3 &amp;= \\frac{255}{512} &amp;&amp;= \\frac{2^8-1}{2^9}, \\\\ &amp; \\phantom{1111} \\vdots \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"153\" height=\"210\" />\nBy induction, it can be proven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a8e73fc37a99f578a0d48bdd10983cc866195da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u_k=\\frac{2^{2^k}-1}{2^{2^k+1}}=\\frac12-\\frac{1}{2^{2^k+1}}.\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"42\" />\nWe substitute this into the inequality, then solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddfbb7689d099f701930562aa20ff8d6cf8566b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k:$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23ec2370f2e4aea9d84dde03ffc869dae237844d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac12-\\frac{1}{2^{1000}} &amp;\\leq \\frac12-\\frac{1}{2^{2^k+1}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2^{1000}} &amp;\\leq -\\frac{1}{2^{2^k+1}} \\\\ 2^{1000} &amp;\\leq 2^{2^k+1} \\\\ 1000 &amp;\\leq 2^k+1. \\end{align*}\" width=\"176\" height=\"135\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17e3384a6e695234c2f84815eddc3fdc9fa76672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^9+1 \\leq 1000 \\leq 2^{10}+1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"20\" /> the least such value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e6a0f1c18703d8a591bf4c0e68ba8a1a19de1a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\: 10}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we list out the first few values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we get the series <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b6ced287a3a2681fc568e76e0f71beef507db85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{3}{8}, \\frac{15}{32}, \\frac{255}{512}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" />, which always seems to be a negative power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> away from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. We can test this out by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/641947256d5bdcdd2f6b774382cd6e28fd1055b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_k=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2^{n_k}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41ab99b0f58dae6c695a874ea60322f89e49f17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_0=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4371e1dbd513a4732e655ecf12557a911f2fc4b4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} u_{k+1} &amp;= 2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2^{n_{k}}}\\right)-2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2^{n_{k}}}\\right)^2 \\\\ &amp;= 1-\\frac{1}{2^{n_k - 1}}-2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2^{n_k}}+\\frac{1}{2^{2 \\cdot n_k}}\\right)\\\\ &amp;= 1-\\frac{1}{2^{n_k - 1}}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2^{n_k-1}}-\\frac{1}{2^{2 \\cdot n_k-1}} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2^{2 \\cdot n_k-1}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"330\" height=\"182\" />\nThis means that this series approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, as the second term is decreasing. In addition, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2118bffd6b3625eff0980f129cbed867793ac0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{k+1}=2 \\cdot n_k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>We claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/0134e85f21813a927be1b53a73e4eb2694881a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_k = 2^k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />, which can be proven by induction:\n</p><p><u><b>Base Case</b></u>\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/940c7b14b95334a89f13e4fd2abb5d9fc46e6853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_0=2=2^0+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><u><b>Induction Step</b></u>\n</p><p>Assuming that the claim is true, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe062a4806d651230c32013a716658b12c6ae7c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{k+1}=2 \\cdot (2^k+1)-1=2^{k+1}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/630e636f87a475692f95094823d840abf35422cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{10}=2^{10}+1&gt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/1/631191a79d5521548d8bf4c1b7d715235c3452ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_9=2^9+1&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, the least value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f217a328268b905ad593c484b8b790f24aa6f26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\: 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ConcaveTriangle\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58f4223020d3964ce8d772668ef19cc8571efb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_{k+1} = 2u_k - 2{u_k}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"21\" />. Multiply this equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from both sides. The equations can then be written nicely as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/adac952f312499efd49012b891867ad5702307ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2u_{k+1} - 1 = -(2u_k-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"197\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a9275788168da0ad35ff788f5812cb355a7cb19e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_k = 2u_k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18f75e06656520a48476d7a452c99a77a0b95402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_{k+1} = -(v_k)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/310f89a2e7a2f1c934a77aefa6ef18b0bc73d7bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_0 = 2u_0 - 1 = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />. Since the magnitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/3/a03736fe3d54aefeb282b0bd55d83d70178e1d8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and because our recursive relation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91b07738b87e0e63f03a32d0dee47bbe5ce9b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> squares the previous term (and negates it), we see that as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99d629b21b6ddeb46b45ce8969eba0be3401549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\rightarrow \\infty, 2u_k - 1 = v_k \\rightarrow 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d991eb29bd944cc7eaa2c145f00f6dda18a8745a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_k \\rightarrow \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/6383ce6c1e6e48a90425beb4dfb713aa75b2e78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Isolating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/569d3bf9897228340b96bde81f593537eb8ba733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> in our relation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c4f6c75a7ccb7f31d10fb16fa76e0854f34539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2u_k - 1 = v_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b57463e41906d75abce5b56400fe873b1460305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_k = \\frac{v_k + 1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />.\nSubstituting into the inequality, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8e9c2236d7e5b49c94ee90039a97a954fd4f73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|\\frac{v_k + 1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\right| \\le \\frac{1}{2^{1000}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"166\" height=\"45\" />. Rewriting this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615a82bc66108cf48ca01df1548bb4370693ebb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|v_k| \\le \\frac{1}{2^{999}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da27b29723ba15e10f7e7e84c401d5d601741a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{v_k\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> is much easier to handle because of its simple recursive relation. Writing out a few terms shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae2381ddddc7cbdb3d04365b9bc005bb26ea426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|v_k| = \\frac{1}{2^{2^k}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />. Now it just comes down to having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/a/7aad940a48c5ad919d4f34c991e9aa0e648cb4b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k &gt; 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c3008d2ce99ac79ba36eedba89114ff2830510f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\: 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~chezpotato\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZfHql_vhNes\">https://youtu.be/ZfHql_vhNes</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B\">2021 Fall AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2021 Fa